      "content": "For a more standard, welcoming vibe, consider neighborhoods like Soho or Shoreditch for their iconic energy and tourist amenities, while observing that Camden Town can feel unexpectedly lively and chaotic for first-time visitors. Areas north of the main tube lines, such as parts of zones 4 and 5 near Bethnal Green or Mile End, often have a different local demographic and higher crime rates, so proceed with extra caution or stay in well-frequented pubs instead. Ultimately, cities like London thrive on their unpredictable character, so even \"chill\" zones can shift at night, making it wise to keep your eyes open regardless of your chosen area.",
